 $q$Deamination in the liver converts surplus amino groups into urea, which the kidneys filter out. Glucose and salts are reabsorbed, not excreted as waste.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('biology','genetics',2016,1, $q$In the F₂ generation of a monohybrid cross, the genotype ratio is$q$,
