 $q$The placenta is the exchange surface: nutrients and oxygen in, urea and carbon dioxide out — while keeping the two blood systems mostly separate.$q$,
 'single', null, 1),
('biology','cellular-processes',2022,1, $q$Follow the light-dependent stage of photosynthesis: identify what chlorophyll does, what is split to release oxygen, and where the products go next.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"Carbon dioxide splits, releasing oxygen"},{"label":"B","text":"Water is split (photolysed), releasing oxygen"},{"label":"C","text":"Glucose absorbs light and breaks down"},{"label":"D","text":"Oxygen reacts with starch to release energy"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$All the oxygen that ever left a leaf came from water molecules, split at the thylakoid membrane — confirmed elegantly by isotope-tracing experiments.$q$,
