 'single', null, 1),
('biology','excretion-nerve',2022,3, $q$The sequence of structures in a simple reflex arc is$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"effector → motor neurone → CNS → sensory neurone → receptor"},{"label":"B","text":"receptor → sensory neurone → CNS → motor neurone → effector"},{"label":"C","text":"sensory neurone → effector → receptor → CNS → motor neurone"},{"label":"D","text":"CNS → receptor → sensory neurone → motor neurone → effector"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$Signal flows: receptor detects → sensory neurone carries in → CNS relay decides → motor neurone carries out → effector responds. Reflexes bypass conscious thought, which is why they are fast.$q$,
