('biology','evolution',2025,2, $q$The pentadactyl limbs of humans, bats and whales are cited as evidence for evolution because they are$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"analogous structures"},{"label":"B","text":"homologous structures inherited from a common ancestor"},{"label":"C","text":"unrelated by ancestry"},{"label":"D","text":"vestigial organs"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$Same underlying bone plan, different functions — homology points to common ancestry. Analogous structures (wings of bat and insect) instead indicate convergent evolution.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('biology','systems',2025,3, $q$The pigment in red blood cells responsible for transporting oxygen is$q$,
