('english','lexis-structure',2004,21, $q$Fill each gap with the most appropriate option: Either the coach or the players ___ to blame for the defeat.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"is"},{"label":"B","text":"was"},{"label":"C","text":"are"},{"label":"D","text":"has"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$With 'either ... or', the verb agrees with the subject nearer to it ('the players', plural), so the plural verb is correct.$q$,
