('biology','cellular-processes',2000,33, $q$A destarched potted plant is exposed to sunlight with one leaf enclosed in a jar containing soda lime, while a control leaf is enclosed in a similar jar without soda lime. After several hours, iodine testing shows starch in the control leaf but none in the treated leaf. The conclusion is that$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"light is unnecessary for photosynthesis"},{"label":"B","text":"carbon dioxide is necessary for photosynthesis"},{"label":"C","text":"the leaf stores oxygen in the dark"},{"label":"D","text":"chlorophyll is destroyed by darkness"}]$o$,
