 $q$Deoxygenated blood leaves the right ventricle through the pulmonary artery to the lungs, and returns by the pulmonary vein to the left atrium. The aorta and pulmonary vein make no part of this outward journey.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('biology','cell-structure',2009,11, $q$Which organelle is known as the powerhouse of the cell because it releases energy for cellular work?$q$,
