('biology','genetics',2009,35, $q$Two heterozygous black guinea pigs (Bb × Bb) are mated. What phenotypic ratio is expected in their offspring?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"3 black : 1 brown"},{"label":"B","text":"2 black : 2 brown"},{"label":"C","text":"1 black : 1 brown"},{"label":"D","text":"4 black : 0 brown"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$Each parent produces B and b gametes in equal numbers. The four equally likely combinations (BB, Bb, Bb, bb) give three black to one brown offspring on average.$q$,
 'multi',
 $st$[{"title":"Gametes","kind":"text","content":"Each heterozygous parent (Bb) makes two types of gamete, B and b, in equal numbers.","note":"Black (B) is dominant over brown (b)."},{"title":"Combination grid","kind":"math","content":"Crossing the gametes gives four equally likely genotypes: BB, Bb, Bb and bb.","note":"Punnett square of a monohybrid cross."},{"title":"Phenotypes","kind":"text","content":"Every offspring carrying at least one B allele (BB or Bb) is black; only bb individuals are brown.","note":"Genotype ratio 1 BB : 2 Bb : 1 bb."},{"title":"Ratio","kind":"text","content":"Three of the four possible outcomes are black and one is brown, hence 3 black : 1 brown.","note":"This is the classic Mendelian 3:1 monohybrid ratio."}]$st$,
 3),
('biology','evolution',2009,36, $q$Remains of organisms preserved in sequentially deposited rock layers, which reveal that life has changed gradually over time, are called$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"vestigial organs"},{"label":"B","text":"analogous organs"},{"label":"C","text":"mutants"},{"label":"D","text":"fossils"}]$o$,
