('biology','cellular-processes',2012,16, $q$When a plant cell is placed in a strong salt solution, it becomes plasmolysed because$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"salt moves into the cell sap"},{"label":"B","text":"the cell wall draws water in"},{"label":"C","text":"water passes out of the cell sap into the more concentrated external solution"},{"label":"D","text":"the cytoplasm pumps salt out actively"}]$o$,
