('biology','systems',2012,24, $q$Which sequence correctly follows inspired air through the respiratory system of man down to the point of gaseous exchange?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"alveoli → bronchioles → bronchi → trachea"},{"label":"B","text":"nostrils → alveoli → trachea → bronchi"},{"label":"C","text":"nostrils → trachea → bronchi → bronchioles → alveoli"},{"label":"D","text":"nostrils → bronchioles → trachea → bronchi"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$Air entering the nostrils is warmed and filtered, then passes down the trachea, through the bronchi to each lung and along fine bronchioles. The alveoli, at the end of this route, are the sites where oxygen and carbon dioxide are exchanged.$q$,
 'multi',
 $st$[{"title":"Upper passage","kind":"text","content":"Air enters through the nostrils and travels down the trachea.","note":"Cilia and mucus trap dust along the way."},{"title":"Binary division","kind":"text","content":"The trachea branches into two bronchi, one for each lung.","note":"Cartilage rings keep the tubes open."},{"title":"Airway tree","kind":"text","content":"Inside each lung the bronchi divide repeatedly into still narrower bronchioles.","note":"This branching multiplies air passages."},{"title":"Exchange site","kind":"text","content":"Each bronchiole ends in clusters of alveoli, where blood takes up oxygen and releases CO₂.","note":"Only alveoli permit gaseous exchange."}]$st$,
 2),
('biology','ecology',2012,25, $q$All the organisms of different species living and interacting in one habitat at a given time make up a$q$,
