 'single', null, 2),
('biology','cell-structure',2012,26, $q$Which set of structures is present in BOTH plant and animal cells?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"nucleus, mitochondrion and ribosome"},{"label":"B","text":"cell wall and large central vacuole"},{"label":"C","text":"chloroplast and centriole"},{"label":"D","text":"chloroplast and cellulose cell wall"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$Nuclei, mitochondria and ribosomes are universal features of eukaryotic cells. Cell walls, chloroplasts and large vacuoles belong to plant (or green) cells, while centrioles are animal.$q$,
