('mathematics','trigonometry',2004,25, $q$A ship sails 8 km from port P on a bearing of 030° to Q, then 5 km from Q on a bearing of 150° to R. Find the distance PR.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"13 km"},{"label":"B","text":"√89 km"},{"label":"C","text":"8 km"},{"label":"D","text":"7 km"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$At Q the angle between QP (bearing 210°) and QR (bearing 150°) is 60°, so PR² = 8² + 5² − 2(8)(5)cos 60° = 64 + 25 − 40 = 49, giving PR = 7 km.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Find the included angle","kind":"math","content":"QP has bearing 210°; QR has bearing 150°; angle PQR = 60°","note":"The back bearing of PQ is 030° + 180° = 210°"},{"title":"Apply the cosine rule","kind":"math","content":"PR² = 8² + 5² − 2(8)(5)cos 60°","note":"cos 60° = 1/2"},{"title":"Evaluate","kind":"math","content":"PR² = 64 + 25 − 40 = 49, so PR = 7 km","note":"Adding the 2abcos term would give √129"}]$st$, 3),
