('mathematics','geometry',2009,35, $q$Using π = 22/7, find the curved surface area of a cylinder of radius 7 cm and height 10 cm.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"154 cm²"},{"label":"B","text":"220 cm²"},{"label":"C","text":"308 cm²"},{"label":"D","text":"440 cm²"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$The curved surface area is 2πrh = 44 × 10 = 440 cm². Option A is one base area and B is πrh without the factor 2.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"State the formula","kind":"math","content":"CSA = 2πrh, with π = 22/7","note":"The circumference 2πr sweeps out the height to wrap the cylinder."},{"title":"Clear the radius","kind":"math","content":"2 × (22/7) × 7 = 44 (the 7s cancel)","note":"Dropping the factor 2 here is the classic slip."},{"title":"Multiply by the height","kind":"math","content":"44 × 10 = 440 cm²","note":"154 cm² would be a single base area (πr²), and 220 cm² would be πrh without the 2."}]$st$,
 3),
('mathematics','geometry',2009,36, $q$Find the determinant of the matrix [[3, 4], [5, 6]].$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"2"},{"label":"B","text":"-2"},{"label":"C","text":"-38"},{"label":"D","text":"38"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$The determinant of [[a, b], [c, d]] is ad - bc = 3 × 6 - 4 × 5 = 18 - 20 = -2.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','geometry',2009,37, $q$A chord 24 cm long is 5 cm from the centre of a circle. Find the radius of the circle.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"12 cm"},{"label":"B","text":"17 cm"},{"label":"C","text":"13 cm"},{"label":"D","text":"5 cm"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$The perpendicular from the centre bisects the chord, so the radius is √(12² + 5²) = 13 cm. Adding 12 and 5 gives the tempting 17.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Bisect the chord","kind":"math","content":"Half of the chord = 24 ÷ 2 = 12 cm","note":"The perpendicular from the centre to a chord bisects it."},{"title":"Apply Pythagoras","kind":"math","content":"radius² = 12² + 5² = 144 + 25 = 169","note":"The radius is the hypotenuse, not 12 + 5 = 17."},{"title":"Take the square root","kind":"math","content":"radius = √169 = 13 cm","note":"This is the 5-12-13 right triangle."}]$st$,
 3),
('mathematics','statistics',2009,38, $q$In a class of 40 students, 25 offer Biology and 20 offer Chemistry. If 8 students offer neither subject, how many offer both?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"5"},{"label":"B","text":"15"},{"label":"C","text":"12"},{"label":"D","text":"13"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$Students offering at least one subject: 40 - 8 = 32. By inclusion-exclusion, both = 25 + 20 - 32 = 13.$q$,
 'single', null, 2);

