('mathematics','geometry',2010,29, $q$Find the inverse of the matrix [[2, 1], [3, 4]].$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"(1/5)[[4, 1], [3, 2]]"},{"label":"B","text":"(1/5)[[4, -3], [-1, 2]]"},{"label":"C","text":"(1/5)[[2, -3], [-1, 4]]"},{"label":"D","text":"(1/5)[[4, -1], [-3, 2]]"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$The determinant is 2 × 4 - 1 × 3 = 5. Swapping the leading diagonal and negating the other two entries gives (1/5)[[4, -1], [-3, 2]].$q$,
