('mathematics','trigonometry',2012,26, $q$A boy walks 5 km from P on a bearing of 020° to Q, then 12 km from Q on a bearing of 110° to R. Find |PR|.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"17 km"},{"label":"B","text":"7 km"},{"label":"C","text":"13 km"},{"label":"D","text":"25 km"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$The bearings differ by 90°, so the path turns through a right angle at Q. Then |PR| = √(5² + 12²) = 13 km.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Check the turn","kind":"math","content":"Bearing change: 110 - 20 = 90°, so the angle at Q is a right angle","note":"When two bearings differ by exactly 90°, the displacement triangle is right-angled."},{"title":"Apply Pythagoras","kind":"math","content":"|PR|² = 5² + 12² = 25 + 144 = 169","note":"The five known right-triangle triples include 5-12-13."},{"title":"Take the root","kind":"math","content":"|PR| = √169 = 13 km","note":"17 is only 5 + 12 added, and 7 is 12 - 5 subtracted."}]$st$,
 3),
