('mathematics','calculus',2014,34, $q$Evaluate ∫ (6x⁴ + 3x)/x dx.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"(3/2)x⁴ + 3x + C"},{"label":"B","text":"(3/2)x⁴ + x + C"},{"label":"C","text":"6x⁴ + 3x + C"},{"label":"D","text":"(3/2)x⁴ + C"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$Divide first: (6x⁴ + 3x)/x = 6x³ + 3. Integrating gives (3/2)x⁴ + 3x + C; option D drops the constant's integral 3x.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','calculus',2014,35, $q$A particle moves along a line such that its displacement is s = t³ - 6t² + 9t. Find the times at which its velocity is zero.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"t = 1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"t = 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"t = 1 and t = 3"},{"label":"D","text":"t = -1 and t = -3"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$Velocity v = 3t² - 12t + 9 = 3(t - 1)(t - 3), which vanishes at t = 1 s and t = 3 s.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Differentiate for velocity","kind":"math","content":"v = ds/dt = 3t² - 12t + 9","note":"Velocity is the rate of change of displacement."},{"title":"Factorise","kind":"math","content":"v = 3(t² - 4t + 3) = 3(t - 1)(t - 3)","note":"Extract the common factor 3 before factorising, or the roots still come out the same."},{"title":"Solve v = 0","kind":"math","content":"t = 1 s and t = 3 s","note":"Both roots are within the motion; stopping once short misses the turn at t = 3."}]$st$,
 3),
('mathematics','quadratics',2014,36, $q$Find k if (x + 2) is a factor of x³ + kx - 20.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"14"},{"label":"B","text":"28"},{"label":"C","text":"-14"},{"label":"D","text":"-28"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$By the factor theorem, P(-2) = -8 - 2k - 20 = 0, so 2k = -28 and k = -14. Substituting +2 instead of -2 gives +14.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','progressions',2014,37, $q$The 3rd and 8th terms of an A.P. are 15 and 30 respectively. Find the first term.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"15"},{"label":"B","text":"3"},{"label":"C","text":"21"},{"label":"D","text":"9"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$a + 2d = 15 and a + 7d = 30, so subtracting gives 5d = 15, d = 3. Then a = 15 - 6 = 9, and option C is the 5th term.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Translate each condition","kind":"math","content":"a + 2d = 15 and a + 7d = 30","note":"Term number n contributes (n - 1) multiples of d."},{"title":"Eliminate a","kind":"math","content":"(a + 7d) - (a + 2d) = 5d = 15, so d = 3","note":"The gap of 5 positions carries all 5 multiples of d."},{"title":"Recover a","kind":"math","content":"a = 15 - 2(3) = 9","note":"Substitute into either equation to confirm: 9 + 7(3) = 30."}]$st$,
 3),
('mathematics','geometry',2014,38, $q$A circle has radius 13 cm and a chord 10 cm long. How far is the chord from the centre?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"3 cm"},{"label":"B","text":"10 cm"},{"label":"C","text":"23 cm"},{"label":"D","text":"12 cm"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$Half the chord is 5 cm, and d² = 13² - 5² = 144, so d = 12 cm, completing the 5-12-13 triangle. Subtracting 13 - 10 gives the distractor 3.$q$,
 'single', null, 2);

