('mathematics','trigonometry',2017,20, $q$From a point A on level ground, the angle of elevation of the top of a vertical tower is 30°. From a point B which is 48 m closer to the foot of the tower along the same straight line, the angle of elevation is 60°. Find the height of the tower.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"12√3 m"},{"label":"B","text":"24 m"},{"label":"C","text":"24√3 m"},{"label":"D","text":"48√3 m"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$With h = d√3 from B and h = (d + 48)/√3 from A, equating heights gives 3d = d + 48, so d = 24 m. The height is h = 24√3 m.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Set up the two triangles","kind":"scene","content":"Let d be the distance from B to the foot of the tower. From B, h = d tan 60° = d√3. From A, a distance d + 48 away, h = (d + 48) tan 30° = (d + 48)/√3.","note":"The same height h is seen from two distances."},{"title":"Equate the two expressions for h","kind":"math","content":"d√3 = (d + 48)/√3 → 3d = d + 48 → d = 24 m","note":"Multiply both sides by √3."},{"title":"Compute the height","kind":"math","content":"h = 24√3 m (about 41.6 m)","note":"Substitute d = 24 into h = d√3."}]$st$, 3),
('mathematics','trigonometry',2017,21, $q$Without using tables, evaluate sin 30° + cos 60°.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"½"},{"label":"B","text":"√3"},{"label":"C","text":"1"},{"label":"D","text":"2"}]$o$,
