('mathematics','statistics',2017,27, $q$The masses of 30 bags of rice are grouped as: 1–5 kg (3 bags), 6–10 kg (8 bags), 11–15 kg (12 bags), 16–20 kg (6 bags) and 21–25 kg (1 bag). Calculate the mode of the distribution.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"10.5 kg"},{"label":"B","text":"11.0 kg"},{"label":"C","text":"12.0 kg"},{"label":"D","text":"12.5 kg"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$The modal class is 11–15 kg with frequency 12. Using the boundary 10.5, the mode is 10.5 + (4/10) × 5 = 12.5 kg.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Identify the modal class","kind":"text","content":"The highest frequency is 12, so the modal class is 11–15 kg.","note":"The mode lies inside this class."},{"title":"State the formula values","kind":"math","content":"L = 10.5, f = 12, f₁ = 8, f₂ = 6, c = 5","note":"The lower boundary of the class 11–15 is 10.5."},{"title":"Substitute and evaluate","kind":"math","content":"Mode = 10.5 + (12 − 8)/((12 − 8) + (12 − 6)) × 5 = 10.5 + 2 = 12.5 kg","note":"(f − f₁) = 4 and (f − f₂) = 6."}]$st$, 2),
('mathematics','statistics',2017,28, $q$In a class of 40 students, 25 study Mathematics, 20 study Physics and 8 study neither subject. How many study both?$q$,
