('mathematics','number-surds',2018,12, $q$Solve the equation |x − 3| = 2x + 1.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"x = 2/3"},{"label":"B","text":"x = −4"},{"label":"C","text":"x = 4"},{"label":"D","text":"x = 1/3"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$Taking x − 3 = 2x + 1 gives x = −4, which fails the check since |−4 − 3| = 7 but 2(−4) + 1 = −7. Taking −(x − 3) = 2x + 1 gives x = 2/3, and |2/3 − 3| = 7/3 = 2(2/3) + 1, so only x = 2/3 holds.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','number-surds',2018,13, $q$The compound interest on a certain sum for 1 year at 8% per annum is ₦1,256. Find the sum.$q$,
