('mathematics','progressions',2020,17, $q$Find the sum of all the integers from 1 to 100 that are divisible by 3.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"1683"},{"label":"B","text":"1716"},{"label":"C","text":"1618"},{"label":"D","text":"1731"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$The terms form the AP 3, 6, ..., 99 with 33 terms. The sum is 33/2 × (3 + 99) = 33 × 51 = 1683.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Count the terms","kind":"math","content":"The multiples of 3 from 1 to 100 are 3, 6, ..., 99, and 99/3 = 33 gives n = 33 terms.","note":"The last multiple of 3 below 100 is 99."},{"title":"Apply the sum formula","kind":"math","content":"S = n/2 (first + last) = 33/2 × (3 + 99) = 33 × 51 = 1683","note":"Pairing first and last terms helps."},{"title":"State the total","kind":"text","content":"The integers divisible by 3 between 1 and 100 add up to 1683.","note":"The average term is 51, and 51 × 33 = 1683."}]$st$, 2),
('mathematics','progressions',2020,18, $q$The second and fourth terms of a geometric progression are 6 and 24 respectively. Find the fifth term if the common ratio is positive.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"48"},{"label":"B","text":"40"},{"label":"C","text":"32"},{"label":"D","text":"64"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$From ar³ = 24 and ar = 6, dividing gives r² = 4, so r = 2 and a = 3. The fifth term is ar⁴ = 3 × 16 = 48.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','progressions',2020,19, $q$A car dealer bought a second-hand car for ₦12,000 and spent ₦3,000 on repairs. If he sold the car for ₦18,000, find his percentage profit.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"15%"},{"label":"B","text":"25%"},{"label":"C","text":"20%"},{"label":"D","text":"30%"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$The total cost is ₦15,000, giving a profit of ₦18,000 − ₦15,000 = ₦3,000. Percentage profit = 3000/15000 × 100 = 20%.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Add up the total cost","kind":"math","content":"Cost = ₦12,000 + ₦3,000 = ₦15,000","note":"Repairs are part of the cost price."},{"title":"Compute the profit","kind":"math","content":"Profit = ₦18,000 − ₦15,000 = ₦3,000","note":"Selling price minus total cost."},{"title":"Express profit as a percentage","kind":"math","content":"Percentage profit = 3000/15000 × 100 = 20%","note":"Divide by the cost price, not the selling price."}]$st$, 2),
('mathematics','quadratics',2020,20, $q$Find the coordinates of the minimum point of the curve y = x² − 6x + 11.$q$,
