('mathematics','statistics',2021,30, $q$Find the variance of the data 2, 4, 6, 8, 10.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"6"},{"label":"B","text":"8"},{"label":"C","text":"32"},{"label":"D","text":"2.8"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$The deviations from the mean 6 are −4, −2, 0, 2 and 4, so the squared deviations total 16 + 4 + 0 + 4 + 16 = 40. The variance is 40/5 = 8. The standard deviation would be 2√2.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Find the mean","kind":"math","content":"mean = (2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + 10)/5 = 6","note":"The sum of the data is 30."},{"title":"Square the deviations","kind":"math","content":"(−4)² + (−2)² + 0² + 2² + 4² = 16 + 4 + 0 + 4 + 16 = 40","note":"Each deviation is measured from 6."},{"title":"Divide by the count","kind":"math","content":"variance = 40/5 = 8","note":"Variance is the mean of the squared deviations."}]$st$, 2),
('mathematics','statistics',2021,31, $q$The heights of 40 seedlings are grouped: 0–5 cm (4 seedlings), 5–10 cm (10 seedlings), 10–15 cm (16 seedlings), 15–20 cm (8 seedlings) and 20–25 cm (2 seedlings). In which class does the median height lie?$q$,
