('mathematics','progressions',2025,16, $q$An arithmetic progression of 10 terms has first term 9 and last term 69. Find the sum of the terms.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"355"},{"label":"B","text":"390"},{"label":"C","text":"400"},{"label":"D","text":"780"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$Sₙ = n/2 (first + last) = 10/2 × (9 + 69) = 5 × 78 = 390.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','progressions',2025,17, $q$The fourth term of a geometric progression is 54 and the common ratio is 3. Find the first term.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"3"},{"label":"B","text":"6"},{"label":"C","text":"18"},{"label":"D","text":"2"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$Since T₄ = ar³ = 27a = 54, we get a = 2. The terms run 2, 6, 18, 54.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','progressions',2025,18, $q$Find the sum of the first 15 terms of the arithmetic progression 7, 10, 13, ...$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"390"},{"label":"B","text":"405"},{"label":"C","text":"420"},{"label":"D","text":"435"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$With a = 7 and d = 3, S₁₅ = 15/2 [2(7) + 14(3)] = 15/2 × 56 = 420. The 15th term itself is 7 + 42 = 49.$q$,
 'multi', $st$[{"title":"Identify a and d","kind":"text","content":"The progression 7, 10, 13, ... has first term a = 7 and common difference d = 3.","note":"The list increases by 3 each time."},{"title":"Apply the sum formula","kind":"math","content":"S₁₅ = 15/2 [2a + 14d] = 15/2 × (14 + 42) = 15/2 × 56","note":"Use Sₙ = n/2 [2a + (n − 1)d]."},{"title":"Compute","kind":"math","content":"S₁₅ = 15 × 28 = 420","note":"56/2 = 28 reduces the arithmetic."}]$st$, 2),
('mathematics','quadratics',2025,19, $q$Solve the equation x² = 2x + 24.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"x = −6 or 4"},{"label":"B","text":"x = 4 or 6"},{"label":"C","text":"x = −4 or −6"},{"label":"D","text":"x = 6 or −4"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$Rearrange to x² − 2x − 24 = 0, then factorize: (x − 6)(x + 4) = 0. Hence x = 6 or x = −4. Check: 6² = 36 = 12 + 24.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','quadratics',2025,20, $q$Find the maximum value of y = −x² + 4x + 1.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"1"},{"label":"B","text":"4"},{"label":"C","text":"5"},{"label":"D","text":"8"}]$o$,
 'C',
 $q$dy/dx = −2x + 4 = 0 gives x = 2, where y = −4 + 8 + 1 = 5. The negative x² coefficient confirms a maximum.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','quadratics',2025,21, $q$The sum of two numbers is 12 and their product is 35. Find the positive difference between the numbers.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"2"},{"label":"B","text":"1"},{"label":"C","text":"3"},{"label":"D","text":"4"}]$o$,
 'A',
 $q$The numbers satisfy x² − 12x + 35 = 0, which factorizes as (x − 5)(x − 7) = 0. The numbers are 5 and 7, differing by 2.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','trigonometry',2025,22, $q$Evaluate sin 45° cos 45°.$q$,
