 'D',
 $q$Each factor is √2/2, so the product is 2/4 = ½. The double angle identity gives sin 90°/2 = ½ as a check.$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','trigonometry',2025,23, $q$A ladder 10 m long leans against a vertical wall, with its foot making an angle of 60° with the ground. How high up the wall does it reach?$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"10 m"},{"label":"B","text":"5√3 m"},{"label":"C","text":"10√3 m"},{"label":"D","text":"5√2 m"}]$o$,
 'B',
 $q$The height above the ground is 10 sin 60° = 10 × √3/2 = 5√3 m (about 8.66 m).$q$,
 'single', null, 2),
('mathematics','trigonometry',2025,24, $q$Evaluate cos 330°.$q$,
 $o$[{"label":"A","text":"−√3/2"},{"label":"B","text":"½"},{"label":"C","text":"−½"},{"label":"D","text":"√3/2"}]$o$,
 'D',
 $q$330° is in the fourth quadrant, where cosine is positive: cos 330° = cos 30° = √3/2.$q$,
